N2  - Between 0.2 and 4% of all pregnancies in western industrialised countries are complicated by cardiovascular disease (CVD), and the number of patients who develop cardiac problems during pregnancy is increasing. Knowledge of the risks associated with CVD during pregnancy and their management is of pivotal importance for advising patients before pregnancy. © Sherborne Gibbs Limited 2012.
