N2  - We have used the denunciations of the adverse events that had been collected according to the program of the "AOGOI Legal Shield", for a total n. 417, of which n. 290 relating to the activities performed in obstetrics and n. 119 in gynaecology. The most frequent adverse events in obstetrics were: fetal death (n. 96 cases), injuries to the fetus or infant (n. 71 cases) and the unseen fetal malformations (n. 42 case). The death of a pregnant woman occurred in 25 cases. In gynaecology n. 116 claims were reported. N. 56 patients complained for an anatomical injury, n. 8 for a fistula and n. 6 patients had to undergo to a non-scheduled hysterectomy. The death of the patient occurred in n. 13 cases. The highest number of surgical complications (n. 20) occurred after an endoscopic intervention. In n. 9 cases there was a pregnancy after tubal sterilization. In n. 9 cases we noticed the presence of retained instrument inside the surgical site. Through the analysis of the claims we can detect the presence of errors in the techniques, behaviours and structures. Taking into account all this, we can identify the most suitable measures to make it more difficult the repetition of the error. © Copyright 2009, CIC Edizioni Internazionali.
